Here's GA4 and the Meta Pixel for your Next.js site, set up so **neither loads until the visitor opts in**. Retargeting is marketing, so the Meta Pixel needs opt-in. Analytics needs at least notice plus a real choice. Dropping both into `layout.tsx` unconditionally is the pattern the Information Regulator's Direct Marketing Guidance Note (Dec 2024) is read as targeting (s69, s18). I'd rate tracking pixels that fire before consent as a **High** finding in an audit.

I've assumed the **App Router** (`app/`). If you're on the Pages Router, the same components go in `_app.tsx`.

## What I built in, and why

| Default | Reason |
|---|---|
| Nothing from Google or Meta loads before a choice is made; "Reject all" is as prominent as "Accept all" | s69, s11 consent must be voluntary and specific; s18 notice |
| Separate **Analytics** and **Marketing** categories | Consent is per purpose. A visitor can allow GA4 and refuse retargeting. |
| Google Consent Mode defaults set to `denied` before anything else | Belt and braces if GA4 is ever loaded some other way |
| Each choice stored as a consent record (version, wording, timestamp) on your server | s11(2)(a): the burden of proving consent is on you |
| "Cookie settings" link in the footer; withdrawing revokes both tags and clears their cookies | s11(2)(b): withdrawing must be as easy as consenting |
| Page URLs sent with query strings stripped (except `utm_*`) | Stops emails, tokens or names in URLs going to Google/Meta (s10, s19) |
| Meta **Advanced Matching off**; no email or phone sent to the Pixel | Hashed email is still personal information, not anonymisation |
| Google Signals and ad personalisation follow the *marketing* choice, not the analytics one | Keeps analytics consent from silently feeding ads |

> If you have this skill's `registry/` installed, use its consent banner and consent gate components (see `registry/README.md`) instead of the hand-written banner below. They follow the same pattern. The code below is for when you don't.

## 1. Environment

```bash
# .env.local  (these IDs are public by design; never put secrets in NEXT_PUBLIC_*)
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX
NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID=000000000000000
```

## 2. Consent state: `lib/consent.ts`

```ts
// Consent categories. "necessary" is always on and needs no consent, but must be disclosed (s18).
export type Consent = {
  version: string;       // bump when banner wording or vendors change -> everyone is asked again
  analytics: boolean;    // GA4
  marketing: boolean;    // Meta Pixel, retargeting, Google ad features
  decidedAt: string;
};

export const CONSENT_VERSION = '2026-10-18.1';
const KEY = 'consent';

export function readConsent(): Consent | null {
  try {
    const raw = document.cookie.split('; ').find((c) => c.startsWith(`${KEY}=`))?.split('=')[1];
    if (!raw) return null;
    const c = JSON.parse(decodeURIComponent(raw)) as Consent;
    return c.version === CONSENT_VERSION ? c : null; // old version -> ask again
  } catch {
    return null;
  }
}

export function writeConsent(analytics: boolean, marketing: boolean, wording: string): Consent {
  const c: Consent = { version: CONSENT_VERSION, analytics, marketing, decidedAt: new Date().toISOString() };
  // 12 months, first-party, strictly necessary (it only stores the choice)
  document.cookie = `${KEY}=${encodeURIComponent(JSON.stringify(c))}; Max-Age=${60 * 60 * 24 * 365}; Path=/; SameSite=Lax; Secure`;
  window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent<Consent>('consentchange', { detail: c }));

  // s11(2)(a) evidence: record what was shown and chosen. Fire-and-forget.
  navigator.sendBeacon?.(
    '/api/consent',
    new Blob([JSON.stringify({ ...c, wording, sourceUrl: location.pathname })], { type: 'application/json' }),
  );
  return c;
}

/** Strip query strings except campaign tags, so PI in URLs never reaches Google or Meta. */
export function safePageUrl(): string {
  const u = new URL(location.href);
  const keep = new URLSearchParams();
  u.searchParams.forEach((v, k) => { if (k.startsWith('utm_')) keep.set(k, v); });
  u.search = keep.toString();
  u.hash = '';
  return u.toString();
}

/** Remove tracker cookies on withdrawal. */
export function clearTrackerCookies(prefixes: string[]) {
  const host = location.hostname;
  const domains = [host, `.${host}`, `.${host.split('.').slice(-3).join('.')}`, `.${host.split('.').slice(-2).join('.')}`];
  document.cookie.split('; ').forEach((c) => {
    const name = c.split('=')[0];
    if (prefixes.some((p) => name.startsWith(p))) {
      domains.forEach((d) => (document.cookie = `${name}=; Max-Age=0; Path=/; Domain=${d}`));
      document.cookie = `${name}=; Max-Age=0; Path=/`;
    }
  });
}
```

## 3. Banner: `components/ConsentBanner.tsx`

```tsx
'use client';
import { useEffect, useState } from 'react';
import { readConsent, writeConsent } from '@/lib/consent';

const WORDING = {
  intro:
    'We use cookies that are needed for the site to work. With your permission we would also like to use ' +
    'Google Analytics to understand how the site is used, and the Meta Pixel to show you our ads on Facebook ' +
    'and Instagram. Google and Meta process this data outside South Africa.',
  analytics: 'Analytics (Google Analytics 4): page visits and how the site is used.',
  marketing: 'Marketing (Meta Pixel, Google ad features): show you our ads on other sites and apps based on your visit.',
};

export function ConsentBanner() {
  const [open, setOpen] = useState(false);
  const [choose, setChoose] = useState(false);
  const [analytics, setAnalytics] = useState(false); // unticked by default
  const [marketing, setMarketing] = useState(false); // unticked by default

  useEffect(() => {
    if (!readConsent()) setOpen(true);
    const reopen = () => { const c = readConsent(); setAnalytics(!!c?.analytics); setMarketing(!!c?.marketing); setChoose(true); setOpen(true); };
    window.addEventListener('openconsent', reopen);
    return () => window.removeEventListener('openconsent', reopen);
  }, []);

  const save = (a: boolean, m: boolean) => {
    writeConsent(a, m, JSON.stringify(WORDING));
    setOpen(false);
  };

  if (!open) return null;
  return (
    <div role="dialog" aria-modal="false" aria-labelledby="consent-title"
         className="fixed inset-x-0 bottom-0 z-50 border-t bg-white p-4 shadow-lg md:p-6">
      <div className="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-3 text-sm">
        <h2 id="consent-title" className="font-semibold">Cookies on this site</h2>
        <p>{WORDING.intro} See our <a className="underline" href="/privacy#cookies">Privacy and Cookie Notice</a>.</p>

        {choose && (
          <fieldset className="space-y-2">
            <label className="flex gap-2"><input type="checkbox" checked disabled /> Strictly necessary (always on)</label>
            <label className="flex gap-2"><input type="checkbox" checked={analytics} onChange={(e) => setAnalytics(e.target.checked)} /> {WORDING.analytics}</label>
            <label className="flex gap-2"><input type="checkbox" checked={marketing} onChange={(e) => setMarketing(e.target.checked)} /> {WORDING.marketing}</label>
          </fieldset>
        )}

        {/* Reject and Accept get equal weight. No dark patterns. */}
        <div className="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          <button className="rounded border px-4 py-2 font-medium" onClick={() => save(false, false)}>Reject all</button>
          <button className="rounded border px-4 py-2 font-medium" onClick={() => save(true, true)}>Accept all</button>
          {choose
            ? <button className="rounded border px-4 py-2 font-medium" onClick={() => save(analytics, marketing)}>Save choices</button>
            : <button className="rounded border px-4 py-2 font-medium" onClick={() => setChoose(true)}>Choose</button>}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}

/** Put this in your footer so people can change or withdraw consent at any time. */
export function CookieSettingsLink() {
  return <button className="underline" onClick={() => window.dispatchEvent(new Event('openconsent'))}>Cookie settings</button>;
}
```

## 4. Tags, gated: `components/Trackers.tsx`

```tsx
'use client';
import { useEffect, useRef, useState } from 'react';
import { usePathname, useSearchParams } from 'next/navigation';
import { readConsent, safePageUrl, clearTrackerCookies, type Consent } from '@/lib/consent';

const GA_ID = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID!;
const PIXEL_ID = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID!;

declare global {
  interface Window { dataLayer: unknown[]; gtag: (...a: unknown[]) => void; fbq: any; _fbq: any; }
}

function loadScript(src: string) {
  if (document.querySelector(`script[src="${src}"]`)) return;
  const s = document.createElement('script'); s.src = src; s.async = true; document.head.appendChild(s);
}

// Consent Mode: everything denied before any Google code runs.
function initGtagStub() {
  if (window.gtag) return;
  window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
  window.gtag = function gtag() { window.dataLayer.push(arguments); } as any;
  window.gtag('consent', 'default', {
    ad_storage: 'denied', ad_user_data: 'denied', ad_personalization: 'denied', analytics_storage: 'denied',
  });
}

function enableGa(c: Consent) {
  initGtagStub();
  window.gtag('consent', 'update', {
    analytics_storage: 'granted',
    // ad features only if the visitor also accepted marketing
    ad_storage: c.marketing ? 'granted' : 'denied',
    ad_user_data: c.marketing ? 'granted' : 'denied',
    ad_personalization: c.marketing ? 'granted' : 'denied',
  });
  loadScript(`https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=${GA_ID}`);
  window.gtag('js', new Date());
  window.gtag('config', GA_ID, {
    send_page_view: false,                       // we send sanitised page views ourselves
    allow_google_signals: c.marketing,
    allow_ad_personalization_signals: c.marketing,
  });
}

function enableMeta() {
  if (!window.fbq) {
    // Standard Meta base code, run only after marketing consent
    const n: any = (window.fbq = function (...args: unknown[]) { n.callMethod ? n.callMethod(...args) : n.queue.push(args); });
    if (!window._fbq) window._fbq = n;
    n.push = n; n.loaded = true; n.version = '2.0'; n.queue = [];
    loadScript('https://connect.facebook.net/en_US/fbevents.js');
  }
  window.fbq('consent', 'grant');
  window.fbq('init', PIXEL_ID); // no advanced-matching object: we don't send email/phone to Meta
}

function disableAll(prev: Consent | null) {
  window.gtag?.('consent', 'update', {
    analytics_storage: 'denied', ad_storage: 'denied', ad_user_data: 'denied', ad_personalization: 'denied',
  });
  window.fbq?.('consent', 'revoke');
  if (prev?.analytics) clearTrackerCookies(['_ga', '_gid', '_gat']);
  if (prev?.marketing) clearTrackerCookies(['_fbp', '_fbc', '_gcl']);
}

export function Trackers() {
  const [consent, setConsent] = useState<Consent | null>(null);
  const prev = useRef<Consent | null>(null);
  const pathname = usePathname();
  const search = useSearchParams();

  useEffect(() => {
    const apply = (c: Consent | null) => {
      if (prev.current && ((prev.current.analytics && !c?.analytics) || (prev.current.marketing && !c?.marketing))) {
        disableAll(prev.current);
        // A full reload guarantees no tag keeps running after withdrawal.
        if (prev.current) return location.reload();
      }
      if (c?.analytics) enableGa(c);
      if (c?.marketing) enableMeta();
      prev.current = c;
      setConsent(c);
    };
    apply(readConsent());
    const onChange = (e: Event) => apply((e as CustomEvent<Consent>).detail);
    window.addEventListener('consentchange', onChange);
    return () => window.removeEventListener('consentchange', onChange);
  }, []);

  // Page views on client-side navigation, with URLs sanitised.
  useEffect(() => {
    if (!consent) return;
    const page_location = safePageUrl();
    if (consent.analytics) window.gtag?.('event', 'page_view', { page_location, page_title: document.title });
    if (consent.marketing) window.fbq?.('track', 'PageView');
  }, [consent, pathname, search]);

  return null;
}
```

## 5. Wire it into the layout: `app/layout.tsx`

```tsx
import { Suspense } from 'react';
import { ConsentBanner, CookieSettingsLink } from '@/components/ConsentBanner';
import { Trackers } from '@/components/Trackers';

export default function RootLayout({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  return (
    <html lang="en-ZA">
      <body>
        {children}
        <footer>
          <a href="/privacy">Privacy Notice</a> · <CookieSettingsLink />
        </footer>
        <ConsentBanner />
        <Suspense fallback={null}><Trackers /></Suspense>
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

Remove any other GA or Pixel snippet (in `<head>`, `_document`, Google Tag Manager or a plugin), or the gating is pointless.

## 6. Consent record: `app/api/consent/route.ts`

```ts
import { NextResponse } from 'next/server';
import { createHash } from 'crypto';

// s11(2)(a): keep evidence of what was shown and chosen. Append-only.
export async function POST(req: Request) {
  const body = await req.json().catch(() => null);
  if (!body || typeof body.version !== 'string') return NextResponse.json({ ok: false }, { status: 400 });

  const ip = req.headers.get('x-forwarded-for')?.split(',')[0]?.trim() ?? '';
  const record = {
    anon_id: crypto.randomUUID(), // or the user id if logged in
    purposes: { analytics: !!body.analytics, marketing: !!body.marketing },
    notice_version: body.version,
    wording: String(body.wording).slice(0, 4000),
    source_url: String(body.sourceUrl ?? '').slice(0, 512),
    ip_hash: ip ? createHash('sha256').update(ip + process.env.CONSENT_IP_SALT).digest('hex') : null,
    user_agent: req.headers.get('user-agent')?.slice(0, 512) ?? null,
    created_at: new Date().toISOString(),
  };
  await saveConsentEvent(record); // insert into your DB, e.g. privacy.consent_events
  return NextResponse.json({ ok: true });
}
```

If you're on Supabase, use the `privacy.consent_events` table from `registry/popia/supabase/migrations/` (RLS on, insert only from this route with the service role key held server-side).

## 7. Security headers

If you have a Content-Security-Policy, allow only what the tags need:

```
script-src 'self' https://www.googletagmanager.com https://connect.facebook.net;
connect-src 'self' https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://www.facebook.com;
img-src 'self' data: https://www.facebook.com https://*.google-analytics.com;
```

## Settings to change outside the code

**GA4 (Admin):**
- Data retention: set to **2 months** unless you have a reason for longer (s14).
- Google Signals: leave off unless you need cross-device remarketing. If on, it only applies to visitors who accepted marketing (handled above).
- Never send email, phone, names or ID numbers as event parameters or user properties.

**Meta Events Manager:**
- Automatic Advanced Matching: **off**.
- Don't upload customer lists (Custom Audiences) unless those people gave s69 marketing consent or fall under the s69(3) existing-customer exception.
- If you add the Conversions API later, it needs the same marketing consent. Server-side isn't a way around it.

## Paperwork that goes with this

1. **Privacy and cookie notice** (s18): list GA4 and Meta Pixel, what they collect (online identifiers, pages visited, device info), the purpose (analytics; retargeting ads), cookie names and lifetimes (`_ga`, `_fbp`, `_fbc`, `consent`), that the data goes to the US and elsewhere, how to change your choice, and Information Regulator contact details.
2. **Cross-border transfer** (s72): Google and Meta process this data outside SA. Record the s72 ground you rely on (consent, given in the banner wording above, and/or the binding terms in their data processing terms) in your ROPA.
3. **ROPA rows** for GA4 and Meta Pixel: purpose, data sent, operator agreement status (Google Ads Data Processing Terms; Meta's Data Processing Terms / Business Tools Terms), hosting country, s72 basis, retention.
4. **Children**: if your audience includes under-18s, don't retarget them. Talk to an attorney before running behavioural ads at a child audience (s34, s35).

## Test before you ship

- Open the site in a fresh incognito window. In DevTools → Network, filter `google` and `facebook`: **nothing** should load until you click Accept. Application → Cookies should show no `_ga` or `_fbp`.
- Click **Reject all**: still nothing. Click **Cookie settings → allow Analytics only**: GA4 loads, Meta doesn't.
- Withdraw: the page reloads, `_ga`/`_fbp` are gone, and no further requests go out.
- If you've got this skill's scripts available, run `python3 scripts/site_check.py https://yourdomain.co.za --out site-check.md` against the deployed site. It checks for trackers and cookies on first load.

Note: this is engineering and compliance guidance, not legal advice.

## Verdict: don't ship this as written

`decide()` makes a **final credit decision based solely on an automated score**, with no human review, no reasons given, and no way for the applicant to respond. A loan decline has legal consequences and affects the person to a substantial degree, and a credit score is a profile of creditworthiness. That puts it squarely under **POPIA s71**. This is one of the things I have to flag before going further: it needs a human decision on the process, and because it's a credit product, a POPIA attorney (and your NCA compliance person) should sign off before launch.

The fix isn't big. It's mostly a status change, a decision record, a review queue and better SMS copy. You can still make next week if you start now.

## Findings

| # | Severity | Finding | Section | Evidence |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | **High** | Declines are final and solely automated. No human review, no chance to make representations, no explanation of the logic. | s71(1), s71(2), s71(3) | `decide.ts:4-5` (`score < 620 ? 'declined'`, comment `// final, no review`) |
| 2 | **High** | Decline SMS gives no reasons and no next step. s71(3) requires sufficient information about the underlying logic and an opportunity to make representations. | s71(3), s18 | `decide.ts:6` |
| 3 | **High** | No decision record. Nothing stores the score, threshold, model version, main factors, or decision mode. You can't explain a decision, defend it, or answer an access request about it. | s71(3)(b), s17, s23 | `decide.ts:5` only writes `status` |
| 4 | **High** | `score` is a function argument. If this function is reachable from an API route that takes the score from the request, an applicant can approve themselves. Score must be fetched server-side from its source. | s19 | `decide.ts:3` |
| 5 | **Medium** | No authorisation or state check. Any caller can re-decide any application, and a decided application can be overwritten. | s19 | `decide.ts:3-5` |
| 6 | **Medium** | `sms.send(applicationId, ...)` passes the application ID as the destination. Either it's a bug, or there's an implicit lookup. Make the recipient explicit and verified so outcomes don't go to the wrong number (a misdirected decline is a disclosure of credit information). | s19, s22 | `decide.ts:6` |
| 7 | **Medium** | Score accuracy is never checked. A stale or mismatched bureau record (wrong person, old data) would decline someone with no chance to correct it. | s16, s24 | `decide.ts:4` |
| 8 | **Info** | Where does `score` come from? If it's a credit bureau score, NCA s68 limits its use to permitted purposes, and your bureau contract applies. If you build your own score and share it with others, ask the attorney whether that's "credit reporting" needing prior authorisation (s57(1)(c)). | s57(1)(c), s15 | Not in file |
| 9 | **Info** | SMS provider is an operator and probably offshore. Record it in your ROPA with operator agreement and s72 basis. Keep SMS bodies free of amounts, account numbers and reasons. | s20, s21, s72 | `decide.ts:6` |

Outside POPIA, check with whoever owns NCA compliance: a single score threshold is unlikely to be enough on its own for the affordability assessment the NCA expects of credit providers, and the NCA also gives consumers a right to reasons when credit is refused (check the Act for the exact sections and wording).

## How s71 applies here

s71 applies when **all** of these are true. All four are:
- a **decision** about a person: approve or decline the loan
- with **legal consequences or substantial effect**: credit is refused
- based **solely** on automated processing: `score < 620`, nothing else, `// final, no review`
- that builds a **profile**: creditworthiness

It's permitted only under s71(2): in connection with a contract where the applicant's request was met (an **approval** does meet the request), **or** with appropriate measures protecting their interests. Those measures must include (s71(3)):
- (a) an opportunity to **make representations** about the decision, and
- (b) **sufficient information about the underlying logic**.

So approvals are on firm ground. **Declines are not**, unless you add the measures above. The cleanest design: an automated "decline" is never final. It becomes `referred`, the applicant is told the main reasons and invited to respond, and a person with real authority to override makes the final call.

Make the human review meaningful. A reviewer who can't see the inputs, or who approves the model's output without looking, is still "solely automated" in practice.

## Suggested rewrite

### Decision record

```sql
-- s71: record how each decision was made, why, and who reviewed it.
create table credit.decisions (
  id               uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(),
  application_id   uuid not null references credit.applications(id),
  outcome          text not null check (outcome in ('approved','declined','referred')),
  decision_mode    text not null check (decision_mode in ('automated','human_reviewed')),
  model_version    text not null,          -- e.g. 'threshold-620@2026-10-18'
  score            int  not null,
  score_source     text not null,          -- bureau name / internal model, and pull reference
  main_factors     text[] not null,        -- plain language, shown to the applicant
  reviewer_id      uuid,                   -- set when a human decides
  representations  text,                   -- s71(3)(a): what the applicant told us
  created_at       timestamptz not null default now()
);
alter table credit.decisions enable row level security;
alter table credit.decisions force row level security;
-- no client policies: only the server and the credit review role read this
-- Rule: an automated decline is never final. It is 'referred' until a human decides.
```

### `decide.ts`

```ts
// s71: approvals may be automated (the applicant's request is met).
// Adverse outcomes are referred to a human, with reasons and a chance to respond (s71(3)).
import { db } from './db';
import { sms } from './sms';
import { getScore } from './scoring';          // server-side source of truth, never from the request
import { requireRole } from './auth';

const MODEL_VERSION = 'threshold-620@2026-10-18';
const THRESHOLD = 620;

export async function decide(applicationId: string, actor: { id: string }) {
  await requireRole(actor, 'credit_system');   // s19: only the decision service may call this

  const app = await db.applications.get(applicationId);
  if (!app) throw new Error('Application not found');
  if (app.status !== 'submitted') throw new Error(`Already ${app.status}`); // no silent overwrite

  const { score, source, factors } = await getScore(app);   // factors: plain-language reasons
  const meetsThreshold = score >= THRESHOLD;
  const outcome = meetsThreshold ? 'approved' : 'referred';

  await db.transaction(async (tx) => {
    await tx.decisions.insert({
      application_id: applicationId,
      outcome,
      decision_mode: 'automated',
      model_version: MODEL_VERSION,
      score,
      score_source: source,
      main_factors: factors,
    });
    await tx.applications.update(applicationId, { status: outcome });
    if (!meetsThreshold) await tx.reviewQueue.insert({ application_id: applicationId, reason: 'below_threshold' });
  });

  // Send to the verified number on the application. No amounts, scores or reasons in the SMS body.
  const to = app.verifiedMobile;
  if (meetsThreshold) {
    await sms.send(to, 'Good news: your loan application was approved. Log in to view and accept your offer.');
  } else {
    await sms.send(to,
      'We need to take a closer look at your loan application before we decide. ' +
      'Log in to see why and to tell us anything we should consider. A person will review it.');
  }
  return outcome;
}

// Called by a human reviewer. This is the only path to a final 'declined'.
export async function finaliseReview(
  applicationId: string,
  reviewer: { id: string },
  outcome: 'approved' | 'declined',
  notes: string,
) {
  await requireRole(reviewer, 'credit_reviewer');
  const app = await db.applications.get(applicationId);
  if (app?.status !== 'referred') throw new Error('Not awaiting review');

  const last = await db.decisions.latest(applicationId);
  await db.decisions.insert({
    application_id: applicationId,
    outcome,
    decision_mode: 'human_reviewed',
    model_version: last.model_version,
    score: last.score,
    score_source: last.score_source,
    main_factors: outcome === 'declined' ? last.main_factors : [],
    reviewer_id: reviewer.id,
    representations: app.representations ?? null,
  });
  await db.applications.update(applicationId, { status: outcome });
  // Notify the applicant in-app with the reasons and how to complain. Keep the SMS body generic.
}
```

### What the applicant sees in the app (s71(3)(b))

> We couldn't approve your application automatically. The main reasons were: **[factor 1]** and **[factor 2]**. A person will review your application before a final decision. If something is wrong or out of date, or there's anything we should consider (for example a recent pay increase), tell us here within 14 days. [Add information] [Ask for a person to review]
>
> We use an automated credit score as part of our assessment. [How we assess applications]

And on a final human decline, include the reasons, how to dispute bureau information with the bureau, and how to complain to the Information Regulator.

### What the reviewer needs to see

The application, the score and its source, the factors, and the applicant's representations, plus the authority to approve, decline or ask for more information. Track override rates. If reviewers never override, the review probably isn't meaningful.

## Before launch checklist

1. Change the flow so automated declines become `referred` (above). **FIN-06**
2. Add the `credit.decisions` table and write a record for every decision. **AI-07**
3. Fetch `score` server-side; add role checks and the state check. **s19**
4. Fix the SMS recipient; keep SMS bodies generic. **FIN-15**
5. Add a short explanation of automated scoring to the application screen and your privacy notice: that you use it, the main factors, and the right to ask for human review (s18, s71(3)(b)).
6. Write the s71 assessment (one page: decision, effect, profile, s71(2) ground, measures) and keep it with your ROPA.
7. Confirm where the score comes from, and get the attorney's view on NCA use limits (s68) and whether any part of this is credit reporting (s57(1)(c)).
8. Add a test that fails if any code path sets `status = 'declined'` without `decision_mode = 'human_reviewed'`.
9. When the repo is ready, run the scanner (`python3 scripts/popia_scan.py <repo> --format md --out popia-scan.md`). Its AI-002 rule flags automated decisions, and it will catch other issues in the code around this file.

