I'd hold off on this one. A required SA ID number field is the wrong tool for "are these real people" on a recipe app, and it would create POPIA risk without fixing the problem.

## Why not an SA ID number

- **It isn't needed for the purpose (s10, minimality).** You may only collect information that is adequate, relevant and *not excessive* for the purpose. Sharing recipes doesn't need a national identifier, and no law (FICA, tax, payroll, credit) requires you to hold one. "Verify users are real" is a valid purpose, but there are far less invasive ways to meet it.
- **It doesn't actually verify anyone.** A 13-digit number that passes the Luhn check and date validation proves only that someone typed a well-formed number. Valid IDs are easy to generate or copy from a leaked document. Without checking it against Home Affairs (through a paid KYC vendor, usually with a selfie, which is **biometric special personal information**), you get no assurance and all the liability.
- **It's high-risk data.** The ID number encodes date of birth, gender and citizenship status, and it is a unique identifier that enables identity fraud. Holding it means field-level encryption, masking, restricted access, access logging, and a much worse breach if your database ever leaks (s19, s22). Users will also drop off at sign-up when a recipe app asks for their ID.
- **A required field makes it worse.** People who don't want to hand it over can't use the app at all, which makes it hard to argue consent or necessity.

## What I'd build instead (layered, proportionate)

| Layer | What it stops | PI collected |
|---|---|---|
| Email verification (confirm link or OTP) | Fake and typo'd emails, throwaway sign-ups | Email (already needed for the account) |
| Bot protection on sign-up (Cloudflare Turnstile / hCaptcha) | Scripted mass sign-ups | None stored |
| Rate limiting on sign-up and login | Credential stuffing, enumeration | None |
| *Optional, only if spam persists:* phone OTP at first post or comment | Low-effort spam accounts | Mobile number, used only for verification |
| 18+ confirmation or neutral DOB age gate *(only if you want an adult-only service)* | Under-18 sign-ups without parental consent (s34–35) | A checkbox, or DOB if you need it |

Plus normal community tools: report/flag buttons, new-account posting limits, and moderation. Together these do far more to ensure "real people" than an ID number would.

